In commit "rpc: handle malformed jsonrpc 2.0 requests correctly" (02380237ddd2ed6878d7a3b0ae2807cfcf2cd9ff)

Instead of adding a third place that converts a caught error into a reply (with the [batch loop](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/02380237ddd2ed6878d7a3b0ae2807cfcf2cd9ff/src/httprpc.cpp#L172-L179) and the outer catch), it could be simpler to make [`JSONErrorReply()`](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/02380237ddd2ed6878d7a3b0ae2807cfcf2cd9ff/src/httprpc.cpp#L41-L46) do the right thing for 2.0 requests, replacing the `Assume` with the behavior it asserts. Then this `parse()` call can stay as it was, and any error thrown after the version is known gets the 2.0 treatment, not just parse errors. Suggested diff from master:

```diff
--- a/src/httprpc.cpp
+++ b/src/httprpc.cpp
@@ -40,10 +40,17 @@ static bool g_rpc_whitelist_default = false;

 static UniValue JSONErrorReply(UniValue objError, const JSONRPCRequest& jreq, HTTPStatusCode& nStatus)
 {
-    // HTTP errors should never be returned if JSON-RPC v2 was requested. This
-    // function should only be called when a v1 request fails or when a request
-    // cannot be parsed, so the version is unknown.
-    Assume(jreq.m_json_version != JSONRPCVersion::V2);
+    // A request known to be JSON-RPC 2.0 gets the error in the reply with HTTP
+    // success, or no reply if it is a notification. HTTP error statuses are
+    // only returned for 1.x requests and requests whose version is unknown.
+    if (jreq.m_json_version == JSONRPCVersion::V2) {
+        if (jreq.IsNotification()) {
+            nStatus = HTTP_NO_CONTENT;
+            return {};
+        }
+        nStatus = HTTP_OK;
+        return JSONRPCReplyObj(NullUniValue, std::move(objError), jreq.id, jreq.m_json_version);
+    }

     // Send error reply from json-rpc error object
     nStatus = HTTP_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR;
```

This would also help #36753, which currently builds the 2.0 reply for a whitelist denial itself and could just throw the error for both versions.

I tested this diff together with the PR's test changes: `interface_rpc.py`, including the new tests, and `rpc_whitelist.py` pass in a debug build.

